# Script commands (`ScrCmd_*`)

When adding a **new** script opcode, touch these in order and keep indices aligned:

1. **`data/script_cmd_table.inc`** — Add `script_cmd_table_entry SCR_OP_<NAME> ScrCmd_<name>, ...` at the **end** of the table unless you intentionally insert (inserting shifts all later opcodes and breaks existing scripts).
2. **`include/constants/script_commands.h`** — **Do not edit by hand.** It is regenerated by `tools/misc/make_scr_cmd_constants.py` when you build (`Makefile` depends on `script_cmd_table.inc`).
3. **`src/scrcmd.c`** — Implement `bool8 ScrCmd_<name>(struct ScriptContext *ctx)` (or the same signature as neighboring commands). Wire any `ScriptContext` / `VarGet` / `FlagGet` usage like existing commands.
4. **`asm/macros/event.inc`** — Add a `.macro` that emits `.byte SCR_OP_<NAME>` and the correct operand layout (match operand order and widths of similar commands).

After changes, **rebuild** so `script_commands.h` and asm stay in sync. If a command only wraps existing engine code, reuse established wait/end patterns (e.g. how other cmds set `ctx->native` or request effects via `requests_effects` on the table entry).
